# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local build tool cache and signing keys — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tools/README.md documents how to recreate this directory. The working copy may contain
# Android SDK/build-tools, dex-tools, apktool and ROM platform keys for local builds, but
# none of those binaries or credentials belong in the public repository.
# tools/env.sh is tracked on purpose: BUILD.md and both READMEs open with `source tools/env.sh`,
# and it only exports paths — the tools and keys it points at stay ignored.
tools/*
!tools/README.md
!tools/README.zh-CN.md
!tools/env.sh
out/*
!out/.gitkeep
# Locally extracted proprietary build inputs and generated APK artifacts.
build-inputs/
imsmanager-compat/out/
imsmanager-compat/input/
# apktool writes its intermediate tree into the stub-apk source directory during
# `apktool b`; only the hand-authored manifest and smali/ are source.
imsmanager-compat/stub-apk/build/
imsmanager-compat/stub-apk/dist/
rro/out/
*.idsig
*.pk8
*.jks
*.keystore
*.x509.pem
*.key.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Device capture logs — never commit (may contain IMSI, phone numbers, IMEI)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
20[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_*/
*_capture*/
*_logcat*/
*_dmesg*/
logcat_*.txt
dmesg*.txt
kernel_*.txt
dumpsys_*.txt
bugreport*
*.br
*.pcap
*.pcapng
# Media captures the property guide tells testers to pull from /data/vendor/ims —
# these carry call audio, so they stay local like every other device capture.
*.rtpdump
*.pcm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build temporaries
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.bak
*.log
*.orig
*.rej
nohup.out
dexjar.jar
dexjar.jar.out/
out.jar
# Root-anchored: an unanchored classes.dex rule would also match a payload DEX added
# under a package directory, which is exactly the silent exclusion the note below warns about.
/classes.dex
/classes[0-9].dex

# NOTE: smali_out/, libs/*.jar, rro/ and everything under
# proprietary_vendor_samsung_ims/ ARE tracked on purpose — they are the
# deliverables of this repository. Do not add blanket *.apk / *.jar / *.zip
# rules here: they would silently exclude imsservice.apk, imsmanager.jar,
# the RRO overlay and the entire compiled bridge, leaving a repo that
# looks complete but cannot be built or installed from.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IDE & Editor noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*~